 "brief": "UNESCO is reviewing Palestinian-submitted documentation to add Jerusalem sesame bread to its list of intangible cultural heritage of humanity, Shehab Wire reported. Palestine filed the nomination in 2025 as part of a review cycle encompassing dozens of heritage elements from countries worldwide.\n\nThe traditional pastry represents Palestinian culinary heritage and cultural identity. The designation, if approved, would recognize the bread-making practice among UNESCO's protected intangible cultural traditions.",
